# Keep the built harness bundle at LF everywhere. The build (esbuild) emits LF;
# without this, a Windows checkout converts dist to CRLF and then every build
# shows dist/cli.js as "modified" (LF -> CRLF) with zero real content change,
# which made release builds look stale and added noise to every diff. Forcing
# eol=lf on the committed artifacts keeps the working tree matching the build.
plugins/mixshift-ai/harness/dist/* text eol=lf

# The bundle is GENERATED, and is rebuilt+committed only at the release cut (see
# CONTRIBUTING -> "dist/ is release-time, not PR-time"). Marking it generated
# collapses it in GitHub PR diffs and keeps it out of language stats, so a review
# shows the source change instead of 4MB of bundled output.
#
# Deliberately NOT given a merge strategy. `merge=ours` would silently keep one
# side and drop the other, which on a bundle means quietly shipping a build that
# is missing another PR's feature. The correct resolution for a dist conflict is
# always to REBUILD from the merged source, never to pick a side.
plugins/mixshift-ai/harness/dist/* linguist-generated=true
